  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The St. Lucia Employers&#x2019; Federation (SLEF), established in 1959, has evolved to represent employers across various sectors. On May 10, 2023, the Committee of Management approved the need to review and modify the Federation&#x2019;s Constitution and Bylaws due to changes in the business environment and challenges from COVID-19 and the national economic crisis. The SLEF requested ILO assistance to review the SLEF Constitution and Bylaws to improve its operational procedures, governance structure, internal governance, risk mitigation, and institutional capacity.
The review aims to meet the needs of current and future members, ensuring effective and efficient use of institutional capacities. Board members will be trained in Good Governance skills to make necessary changes to the bylaws. This initiative will benefit the Federation and its members by enhancing governance and operational efficiency.</narrative>
  </description>
